 ### Veterinarian directory
 
-<a id="req-vet-001"></a>
+<a id="req-vet-001"></a><a id="req-vet-003"></a><a id="req-vet-004"></a>
 
 The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`.
 
+The directory can be narrowed to the veterinarians who hold a named specialty. On the browser page, naming a specialty in the request address shows only the veterinarians who hold it, still a page at a time, and the page-to-page links carry the chosen specialty so a filtered result stays navigable across pages `[REQ-VET-003]`. The machine-readable veterinarian list is a supported surface and accepts the same filter, returning only the veterinarians who hold the named specialty `[REQ-VET-004]`. On both surfaces the specialty is matched in full and without regard to letter case — a value matching only the start of a specialty name matches nothing; a specialty no veterinarian holds yields an empty veterinarian list rather than an error; and a blank, whitespace-only, or absent specialty returns the directory exactly as it was before the filter existed.
+
+The filter is driven only through the request address in this round. Neither surface gains a form, dropdown, or other page control for it.
+
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the directory is opened, then each name and its specialties are listed a page at a time.
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is shown as having none.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty some veterinarians hold, when the browser page is opened for that specialty, then only those veterinarians are listed, a page at a time.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a filtered result spanning more than one page, when a page-to-page link is followed, then the chosen specialty still applies to the page reached.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty differing from a stored specialty name only by letter case, when the browser page is opened, then it matches; given a value matching only the start of a specialty name, then it matches nothing.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty no veterinarian holds, when the browser page is opened, then the page is shown with an empty veterinarian list rather than an error.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a blank, whitespace-only, or absent specialty, when the browser page is opened, then the full directory is listed as if no specialty were given.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given a specialty some veterinarians hold, when the machine-readable list is requested for that specialty, then only those veterinarians are returned.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given a specialty differing from a stored specialty name only by letter case, when the machine-readable list is requested, then it matches; given a value matching only the start of a specialty name, then it matches nothing.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given a specialty no veterinarian holds, when the machine-readable list is requested, then an empty veterinarian list is returned successfully rather than an error.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given a blank, whitespace-only, or absent specialty, when the machine-readable list is requested, then every veterinarian is returned.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. A veterinarian's specialties are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
-2. **Known defect.** A second route returns the same list in a machine-readable form. Nothing consumes it, and it carries no requirement — see the Superseded list.
+2. The machine-readable veterinarian list, once an unused implementation artifact, is a supported surface again as of 2026-08-23, carrying its first requested capability under `REQ-VET-004`. The withdrawn `REQ-VET-002` id is not reused — see the Superseded list.
+3. No page control for the specialty filter is added in this round; a visible control may come as a follow-up request.
 
-**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
